#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Photos that carry a 3D scene (glb-layers-v1), and the XMP samples of the kinds of phases 2 and 3.

A 3D scene of Immuch360 is a photo, <name>_scene3D.jpg: a JPEG preview with our XMP (Kind VolumetricScene), then,
after the end of the JPEG, a binary glTF of the glb-layers-v1 format, SceneLength bytes long and checked by
SceneSha256 (design: store/m2/ai-immersive-2026-10-26/phase23/design-final-2026-10-27.md, sections 3.1, 8.1, 8.2).
This script writes such files without the app: the tiny one the Dart and the Kotlin tests read
(mobile/test/fixtures/ai_immersive/tiny_scene3D.jpg), and synthetic ones of a chosen size for the measures in the
headset (lot MQ: 60 000, 120 000 and 240 000 triangles, two textures of 4096). It also writes the XMP samples of the
three new kinds, which the Dart writers must give byte for byte (xmp_v1_scene_sample.xmp,
xmp_v1_panorama_sample.xmp, xmp_v1_stereo_panorama_sample.xmp).

glb-layers-v1, as written here and read by GlbReader.kt and glb_reader.dart:
  - one root node at the centre of the camera of the photo (glTF frame: x right, y up, looking towards -z), one child
    node per mesh; at most 8 meshes, each of at most 65 535 vertices (a layer cut in bands of rows beyond that);
  - per mesh one primitive of triangles: POSITION float32 VEC3 with its min and max, TEXCOORD_0 float32 VEC2 (0, 0
    the top left of the texture), indices uint32 (each under 65 536), one material;
  - materials opaque, KHR_materials_unlit, the base colour texture a JPEG held in the buffer (image/jpeg), sampler
    linear and clamped;
  - asset.generator names the maker and scene-v1; extras.immuch360 holds the format, the safe zone, the scale and the
    field of view; KHR_xmp_json_ld holds the main fields of the packet as JSON-LD.

The tiny scene is a fixture for the readers (the gate of the Dart side, GlbReader.kt, the preview of the computers),
not the model of the writer of the app (lot S1), which follows section 8.2 of the design in full: where the app writes
a minimal EXIF APP1 in the JPEG, this file has a JFIF APP0; where the app writes in KHR_xmp_json_ld the same packet as
the XMP (IPTC, sums, Source fields), this file holds only Kind, Pipeline and the description; and it has not been
through the glTF-Validator of Khronos, which S1 runs on the files of the app.

The JPEGs are written by a small baseline encoder made for flat 8 x 8 blocks (every block one colour: only the DC
coefficient, quantised by 1, a 4:4:4 frame): pure Python, so the bytes are the same on every machine, with or
without Pillow, and the colour of each block comes back exactly. Enough for a fixture and for a texture that loads
the GPU like a photo.

  make_scene_fixture.py                    writes the tiny scene and the three samples
  make_scene_fixture.py --check            exit 1 when one of them differs from what this script writes (a CI step)
  make_scene_fixture.py --triangles 120000 --texture 4096 --out /mnt/d/DEV/immuch/ai-immersive/mq/scene_120k_scene3D.jpg
                                           a synthetic scene: two layers sharing the triangles, two textures

Pure Python 3, no package.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import hashlib
import json
import math
import pathlib
import struct
import sys

FIXTURES = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3] / "mobile/test/fixtures/ai_immersive"

